Subject: [PATCH 6.12.y 0/8] can: bcm: backport of 8 patches that failed to
 apply to 6.12-stable

This resubmits "can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer
values" (commit 749179c2e25b95d22499ed29096b3e02d6dfd2b4 upstream),
which failed to apply to the 6.12-stable tree, together with 7
further bcm.c patches from the same upstream series that build on it
and would otherwise fail for the same reason. This is the full set
of 11 upstream bcm.c patches from 7.2-rc3 minus the 3 already queued
by the normal stable process for 6.12 ("can: bcm: defer rx_op
deallocation to workqueue to fix thrtimer UAF", "can: bcm: fix
lockless bound/ifindex race and silent RX_SETUP failure", "can: bcm:
add missing rcu list annotations and operations").

Unlike linux-5.10.y/5.15.y/6.1.y/6.6.y, none of these 8 patches
needed content adaptation for the traffic_flags/RX_LOCAL/RX_OWN
context: 6.12-stable already carries commit
fec846fa7eddf7bb651bf88bd78c7db1410ae3b1 ("can: bcm: add recvmsg
flags for own, local and remote traffic", Jan 2024) as part of its
own baseline (6.12 was cut well after that commit landed), so the
traffic_flags context that made several of these patches conflict on
older branches is already present here. All 8 patches apply cleanly
once the 3 already-queued patches are in place; they were previously
reported as FAILED for that missing-prerequisite reason alone, not
for independent conflicts.

Two patches still needed adaptation for infra not available on
6.12-stable. Patch 5/8 ("add missing device refcount for CAN filter
removal"): upstream uses the netdevice_tracker/netdev_hold()/
netdev_put() debug-tracking infra; replaced with the plain,
always-available dev_hold()/dev_put(), which is functionally
identical for the actual fix (holding a reference across a
concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER) - just without the extra leak-tracking
instrumentation. Patch 8/8 ("track a single source interface for
ANYDEV timeout/throttle ops"): upstream reads skb->dev->reg_state via
READ_ONCE(), which fails to compile here ("error: 'sizeof' applied to
a bit-field") because reg_state is a bit-field member of struct
net_device on this branch; read as a plain field instead, which is
functionally equivalent for this best-effort claim heuristic. Both
adaptations mirror the same fixes made on 5.10.y after actual build
failures were reported there ("error: unknown type name
'netdevice_tracker'" and the reg_state 'sizeof' error); this revision
has been verified with a clean git am against a seeded net/can/bcm.c
and no longer references either problematic construct anywhere in
the result.

This assumes the 3 already-queued bcm.c patches for 6.12-stable have
landed by the time this is applied. If not, please let me know and I
will rebase.

Oliver Hartkopp (8):
  can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer values
  can: bcm: fix CAN frame rx/tx statistics
  can: bcm: extend bcm_tx_lock usage for data and timer updates
  can: bcm: validate frame length in bcm_rx_setup() for RTR replies
  can: bcm: add missing device refcount for CAN filter removal
  can: bcm: fix stale rx/tx ops after device removal
  can: bcm: fix data race on rx_stamp/rx_ifindex in bcm_rx_handler()
  can: bcm: track a single source interface for ANYDEV timeout/throttle
    ops

